FRONT_ACT _ (User Actions on the Frontend)
          |
           -> Profile
             |
              -> Edit Profile
                |
                 -> User modifies any profile fields (gender, sexual preferences, bio, interests with tags, pictures, location, first name, last name, email) through UI form elements.
              -> View Own Profile
                |
                 -> User sees their profile information displayed on the UI.
                 -> User sees counters for profile viewers and likers displayed on their profile.
              -> View Profile Visit History
                |
                 -> User sees a list of profiles that have visited their profile, displayed on a UI page.
          |
           -> View Other User Profile (except for their email address and password)
             |
              -> User sees the other user's profile information displayed on the UI (gender, sexual preferences, bio, interests, pictures, location, first name, last name, fame rating, online status, last seen -  without email and password).
              -> Like/Unlike Profile Picture
              -> Send Text (Chat) (only under connection condition)
              -> Report Fake Account
              -> Block/Unblock User
          |
           -> Browsing
             |
              -> Browse Profiles List
                 -> User sees a list of suggested user profile cards/previews displayed on the page.
                 -> User uses sorting controls to sort profiles by age, location, fame, tags.
                 -> User uses filter controls to filter profiles by age, location, fame, tags.
                 -> User clicks a "Like" button (or similar UI element) on a profile card directly from the browse list.
             |
              -> Interactive Map (Bonus)
                 -> User interacts with a map UI displaying user locations (pins, clusters).
                 -> User clicks on map pins/clusters to view profiles in specific locations.
             |
              -> Advanced Search
                 -> User fills out a search form with criteria fields (age gap, fame gap, location input, tag input).
                 -> User sees search results displayed as sortable/filterable profile cards/previews (similar to browsing).
          |
           -> Chat
             |
              -> Chat
          |
           -> Notifications
             |
              -> View Notifications
                 -> User sees a list of recent notifications displayed in the area/dropdown (e.g., "You received a like!", "X viewed your profile", "New message from Y").
        -> Logout
            -> User is redirected to the login page or homepage and session is ended.




BACK_ACTIONS  _
               |
                -> View Other User Profile
                  |
                   -> Log Profile View
                     |
                      -> When a user views a profile, the visit is added to their visit history (and the viewed profile's viewer list).
               |
                -> Like/Unlike Profile
                  |
                   -> Process "Like"
                     |
                      -> Record "like" action in database.
                      -> Check if it's a mutual "like".
                      -> If mutual and both have profile pictures: Establish "connection" and enable chat.
                      -> Send "Like" notification to the liked user.
                      -> If becomes a connection (mutual like): Send "Like Back" (connection) notification to both users.
                  |
                   -> Process "Unlike"
                     |
                      -> Record "unlike" action in database.
                      -> If users were connected, break the "connection" and disable chat.
                      -> Send "Unlike" (disconnection) notification to both users (or just the unliked user, depending on desired notification logic).
               |
                -> Fame Rating Calculation
                  |
                   -> Calculate fame rating based on likes received, profile views, and potentially other factors (algorithm to be defined).
                   -> Update fame rating in database periodically or on event basis (like received, profile view).
               |
                -> Track User Online Status
                  |
                   -> Update user online status (e.g., when login, logout, or periodically during session).
                   -> Store last seen timestamp.
               |
                -> Handle Report Fake Account
                  |
                   -> Record report in database, associate it with the reported user and reporting user.
                   -> Potentially trigger admin notification or moderation queue.
               |
                -> Handle Block/Unblock User
                  |
                   -> Record block/unblock action in database, establishing a block relationship between users.
                   -> Implement logic to prevent blocked users from interacting (viewing profile, messaging, etc.).
               |
                -> Process Advanced Search Query
                  |
                   -> Receive search criteria from Advanced Search UI.
                   -> Construct database query based on criteria (age gap, fame gap, location, tags).
                   -> Retrieve and return sorted/filtered search results.
               |
                -> Chat Backend Implementation
                  |
                   -> Handle sending and receiving of chat messages via backend.
                   -> Store chat messages in the database, associated with sender and receiver.
                   -> Implement logic for message delivery and persistence.
                   -> Implement new message notification system.
               |
                -> Notification System
                  |
                   -> Store notifications in database, associated with recipient user and notification type.
                   -> Implement real-time notification delivery mechanism (e.g., WebSockets, Server-Sent Events) for:
                     |
                      -> "Like" received
                      -> Profile viewed
                      -> Message received
                      -> "Like" back (connection)
                      -> "Unlike" (disconnection)
               |
                -> Logout
                    -> Invalidate user session.